 style=\"text-align: center;\"><span style=\"color: #000000;\"><strong>Important Question</strong></span></h3>\n<p><strong>Q. Has the RRB NTPC 10+2 Inter Level Exam City Details 2026 been released?<br>\n</strong><strong>Answer.&nbsp;</strong>Yes the RRB NTPC 10+2 Inter Level Exam City Details 2026 has been released.</p>\n<p><strong>Q. When was the RRB NTPC 10+2 Inter Level Exam City Details 2026 officially announced?<br>\n</strong><strong>Answer.&nbsp;</strong>The RRB NTPC 10+2 Inter Level Exam City Details 2026 has issue on <strong>27 April 2026</strong>&nbsp;by RRB.</p>\n<p><span data-teams=\"true\"><strong>Q. When will the RRB NTPC 10+2 UG CBT-I exam be held?</strong><br>\n<strong>Answer.</strong> The RRB NTPC 10+2 UG CBT-I examination will be conducted on <strong>7, 8, 9 May &amp; 13, 14, 15, 16, 20 June 2026</strong>.</span></p>\n<p><strong>Q. Where can I check the RRB NTPC 10+2 Inter Level Exam City Details 2026?<br>\n</strong><strong>Answer.&nbsp;</strong>You can check it on the official RRB website:&nbsp;<strong>indianrailways.gov.in</strong></p>\n<p><strong>Q. What should I search on the website to find the RRB NTPC 10+2 Inter Level Exam City Details 2026?<br>\n</strong><strong>Answer.</strong>&nbsp;Look for&nbsp;<strong data-start=\"731\" data-end=\"797\">“Exam City Details – RRB NTPC Graduate Level Recruitment 2025”</strong>&nbsp;in the notifications list</p>\n<p><strong>Q. What login credentials do I need to download the Admit Card?<br>\n</strong><strong>Answer.&nbsp;</strong>Typically you will need your&nbsp;<strong data-start=\"1045\" data-end=\"1068\">Registration Number</strong>&nbsp;(or Roll Number)&nbsp;<strong data-start=\"1086\" data-end=\"1093\">and</strong>&nbsp;your&nbsp;<strong data-start=\"1099\" data-end=\"1116\">Date of Birth</strong>&nbsp;(or Password) to login.</p>\n<p><span style=\"color: #000000;\"><strong>Q. What is RRB Official Website?<br>\n</strong><strong>Answer. </strong>The Official Website of RRB is https://indianrailways.gov.in/</span></p></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n</div>\n</div>\n</div>\n",
